# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED.
#
# An example harness settings file is tracked on purpose where one exists, because "merging a hook
# does not install one" is the single most expensive lesson in this whole toolkit: a settings file
# nobody can read is indistinguishable from one that is wired correctly. NOTHING UNDER .claude/ IS
# TRACKED HERE. The settings example and the hooks it wires stayed with the toolkit in the split, at
# https://wshallwshall.github.io/claude-multisession/HOOKS.html and its INSTALL.md, so this header
# described a file that has never been in this repository.
#
# THE RULE, not a census, and prospective rather than describing anything here today: anything
# tracked under .claude/ MUST carry `.example.` in its name. The harness loads settings.json and
# settings.local.json only, so an `.example.` file is inert by construction and cannot become a
# control that looks installed. The machine-local files are ignored below.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Machine-local overrides. The convention throughout: anything with `.local.` in its name belongs to
# one checkout on one machine and must never be committed.
*.local.*
.claude/settings.local.json

# Coordination state lives in the git directory (<git-common-dir>/ccx-coord), so it is uncommittable
# by construction and needs no rule here. These are the strays that escape it.
*.log
ccx-doctor-report.*

# Language runtimes a project setup hook may create inside a worktree.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editors and desktops.
.vs/
.vscode/*.local.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.bundle/
Gemfile.lock
_site/
